      "mergeID": "646421abc7402758fb86a1ff",
      "mergedPostDetails": "When the user uses full body, lies on the back (or side), and rotates the head to the side then the whole avatar will jitter a lot.\n\nIt seems to happen whenever the head rotates past a certain angle. Speed is completely irrelevant here. So if someone lies in a position where the head is close to certain angles then their avatar will continuously be all over the place.\n\nThis is a different behaviour from these other reports as in this case even slow movement of head triggers the behaviour and it applies to the entire body (including the head). It may be related though as all of them happen because of the IK:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/full-body-jittering-when-turning-head\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/legs-jitter-remotely-when-shaking-head-full-body",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Full body jitter when lying down",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c0a1d622aa2c64a34785e49",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5cafb371ac3c2b014948f09c|full_name} I'm merging your post as well because it is indeed the same issue. What you're describing is a different method of triggering it that does not require fast movement, but it is the same underlying issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
