      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have tested this extensively. It doesn't matter what headset, or tracking. All jitter remotely when moving their head. Now someone has made a \"fix\" for it, but it requires every user to have unity knowledge as well as upload their own avatar as well as OSC understanding, so it's more of a \"band-aid\" than a fix. \n\nI've a friend who has a quest2 with haritora trackers\n\nA friend with a vive with kinect tracking\n\nA friend with a quest2 with kinect tracking\n\nA friend with a index, with tundra trackers\n\na friend with index, vive AND tundra trackers\n\na friend with vive and vive trackers. \n\nAll circumstances of tracking have this \"jitter\" to anyone else looking at them. \n\nthe only way to \"stop\" it is to open a menu, such as \n\n\"avatars\" or \"worlds\" and then turn your head, and your body stops shaking.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
